    "title": "How the Artemis II crew is making history in voyage around moon",
    "text": "NEWSWhy the Artemis II crew matters historically for moon mission J.D. GallopFlorida TodayMarch 31, 2026Updated April 1, 2026, 10:36 a.m. ETMillions of eyes will be trained above the Space Coast and beyond, watching closely as the Artemis II crew makes its historic, high-powered trek toward the moon. In many ways the crew, who are set to liftoff as early as 6:24 p.m. Wednesday, April 1, is more a reflection of modern international relationships and an America at 250 years old than the stoic-minded astronauts who vaulted to the moon and back in the 1960s and 1970s.",
